{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And you. I will ascend the heavens.</b> An allusion to the haughtiness of the heart." "<b>And I will sit on the mount of assembly.</b> It is Mount Zion, and it is called thus because it is the appointed place of HaShem, as in \"they have burned all Your appointed places\" (Psalms 74:8), and the witness is \"the recesses of the north\" (Psalms 48:3), for so was Zion."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:44.358166525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}